<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colony of Natal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1843–1910</span> · Also known as Natal Colony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Colony of Natal was a British colony on the south-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, annexed in 1843 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> republic of Natalia was taken over, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietermaritzburg">Pietermaritzburg</a> and its port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durban">Durban</a>. Bordering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thukela-river">Thukela River</a>, it developed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> economy using indentured Indian labour. In 1910 it became a province of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colony-of-natal.jpg" alt="Colony of Natal" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Natal_Colony_(1875%E2%80%931910).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
